# Root-lane counts for `-p delphi-runtime --tests`, ALL 17 targets under sudo.
#
# LANE RUN 13 — COUNTS + HYGIENE MINUS FRESHNESS. It was recorded as the full-hygiene run
# closing D0A-R24-01. **D0A-R25-05 withdrew one of its checks, so D0A-R24-01 IS REOPENED.**
#
# What run 13 GENUINELY measured: the counts, the 17/17 producer statuses, the PAM stack
# before and after, the stale-session sweep, the helper digest, the account, bwrap, free
# space. Those stand.
#
# What it did NOT measure, despite the line that said it did: **"these binaries are this
# code."** The procedure's §1 claimed "an unchanged set of hashes after a forced rebuild is
# the proof" while its commands computed NO hashes — `| tail -3` printed three artifact
# PATHS (and masked cargo's exit status, having no `pipefail`), and the forced rebuild went
# to `/dev/null`. So the run may have executed binaries built from an earlier tree, and the
# counts above inherit that doubt. The procedure now hashes the full enumerated set (§2b);
# the next root run re-establishes the claim. This one cannot be repaired after the fact.
#
#   EXECUTED 177 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 182     extractor rc=0
#   producers: 17/17 exited 0                   failures: 0
#   predicted 177/5 at feabc56, committed ALONE and BEFORE the run
#
# EVERY HYGIENE CHECK, CAPTURED SEPARATELY — the procedure's failure mode is a human
# confirming the set rather than each member, so each is recorded with its own evidence.
# R25-05 is the sharper version of that failure: capturing each check separately does not
# help if a check's OUTPUT cannot decide the thing it is captured for.
#
#   account          delphi-tool:x:997:972       (gid 972, not 997 — D0A-R17-02)
#   helper digest    aba0f0ea14b751aa…           INSTALLED == STAGED
#   bwrap            0.11.1
#   free space       /run, target dir, /tmp      all above floor
#   forced freshness NOT MEASURED — withdrawn by D0A-R25-05; see the note above. The line
#                    that stood here claimed an identical executable set from a command that
#                    produced no hashes at all.
#   PAM before       439c1d1521d86e4eb011a927aff659db
#   PAM after        md5sum -c → OK              (class 16, the defect already paid for)
#   stale sessions   none, checked before AND after
#
# THE FIVE SKIPS, each naming its own blocker: b1_daemon_binary (needs --features
# insecure-test-seams), an_unreadable_login_defs (this uid can read a 0000 file),
# pidfd_refuses_a_recycled_pid_barrier (no user namespaces), live_logind_query (standing
# DEFER), a_regular_login_user_is_not_refused (running as root). Three of the five skip
# BECAUSE the run is privileged, so 177 and the unprivileged 157 are OVERLAPPING SETS and
# neither contains the other.
#
# ORDERING IS CONVENTION AGAIN (D0A-R22-01, reopened). `git log` on this file and on
# `.expected` is the only evidence the prediction preceded the measurement — and it is
# evidence only because feabc56 contains that file alone. Nothing enforces it.
EXECUTED=177
SKIPPED=5
